hi I'm Eric Voss and the new Halloween  film is the fright you're looking for  this season that is if your greatest  fear is a gun-wielding woods woman  screaming at you while you're  trick-or-treating I think part of the  reason this 2018 Halloween has been so  successful is the way the movie  recreates the classic imagery and setups  from the original John Carpenter classic  and that includes an intentionally  mysterious ending now I have already  gone into the mysteries of Halloween's  ending and it's secret post-credit  moment in another video definitely go  watch that but we just learned that  there was an alternate ending and we can  actually piece together from leaked  drafts of the old script and deleted  scenes shown in the trailers what that  alternate ending was so let's break it  all down and spoiler warning if you  haven't seen Halloween yet okay as you  know if you've seen the movie Halloween  ends with Laurie Strode Jamie Lee Curtis  confronting Michael Myers in her remote  home in the woods which she fortified a  booby trapped in case he ever escaped  and came after her and the version we  saw Laurie initially sent her daughter  Karen Judy Greer into the panic room  under the kitchen while trying at first  to keep Michael out of the house but he  gets in anyway and Laurie hunts him down  room by room sweeping through and  blocking off every room and they  eventually meet face to face in an  upstairs room which Michael filled with  Laurie's target mannequins here they  both get in a couple nasty hits before  Michael throws her out the window over  the balcony while this is going on  Laurie's granddaughter Alison finally  catches up to the house and joins her  mother Karen down in the panic room  Michael tries to get to them but  Laurie's stabs him from behind Karen  shoots him in the face with her  childhood rifle and the three women  trapped Michael Myers down the panic  room and it's revealed to be a cage of  its own and Laurie torches the house so  Laurie Karen and Alison escape in the  back of a truck meanwhile Michaels body  has never shown suggesting that he could  have once again disappeared into the  night and of course at the end of the  credits you can hear the sound of  Michael breathing fine that's exactly  the case however if you watched every  single trailer shot like a crazy you may  remember a brief shot of Laurie and  Michael engaging in a knife fight in the  yard outside Laurie's home kitchen knife  against kitchen knife this shot was  actually part of the movie's original  ending in we could see what that ending  was by reading a final couple pages of  an old draft of the film script that was  written by Jeff Radley Danny McBride and  David Gordon Green in this alternate  version Alison arrives at Laurie's house  earlier when Laurie is still in the  middle  her confrontation with Michael Myers  downstairs by the front door and Michael  referred to as the shape in the script a  reference to the original credit Nick  castle received in the first movie  appears in the doorway on the front  porch and Laurie fires her last shot of  him but misses this leads to a classic  showdown with Laurie charging Michael  like a mama bear and taking him on  outside where their blades meet Michael  ends up stabbing her in the chest and  Laurie slices his arm he's already  losing blood from when Laurie shot off  his fingers they're both wounded it  could really go either way and in this  alternate version this is where Laurie's  daughter Karen Judy Greer emerges from  the basement panic room actually in this  older draft her name was Shanna or Shana  that was changed to Karen and instead of  her childhood rifle she holds a high  tech crossbow now there's a [ __ ]  missing at this point from the old  script but presumably Shanna  Karen shot Michael with this crossbow  and a woman exchanged some words and  they run out to the road where we see on  page 94 they waved down a truck and then  they escape and this final page leaves  us with Michael alone in the woods among  all the mannequins he sits by a tree and  he touches his wounds breathing  listening to sirens in the distance and  the final words say his breathing  deepens exhausted or possibly his works  okay this sounds like a very clear set  up for a sequel with the final question  being will this still alive Michael  Myers live long enough to kill again  instead of the theatrical version we all  saw leaving us with the question where  the hell is Michael is he alive at all  you'll also notice that well unless they  crammed a lot on that missing page 93 of  the old draft the old version did not  include most of the cool stuff that we  saw in the actual climax of the final  cut Laurie sweeping through the rooms of  the house Laurie fighting Michael in  that room that he filled with her  mannequins Michael throwing Laurie over  the balcony and Laurie stealing his move  from the first movie and pretending to  be dead but then slipping away Karen  pretending to panic and luring Michael  down to the panic room but then shooting  them with the rifle  Laurie jumping out from the shadows  stabbing Michael and the three women  torching the house according to some  unconfirmed statements by people  claiming to have seen test screenings  with the alternate ending the ending  without all this stuff came off as  laughably bad and necessitated a reshoot  to put all this new climactic stuff in  and yeah this is unconfirmed I don't  know which version people actually saw  there's probably a lot of versions that  were tested in front of audiences so we  don't really know if this original  ending was really that bad but this  script does prove that Laurie did  one point faced Michael one-on-one with  the kitchen knife and that Michael  sitting among Laurie's mannequins was at  one point the movies final image not as  we saw a move that Michael made inside  Laurie's house now on the page I  definitely feel the catharsis of Laurie  confronting her mortal enemy with the  same weapon he came after her with all  those years ago the kitchen knife but  the additions to the final theatrical  cut bring even more symbolic reversals  into the film's climax which I go into  super in-depth in my breakdown of the  movie now Laurie's overall defense  against Michael has multiple steps  vindicating each of her seemingly  paranoid precautions around her house  has actually useful and building up to a  fiery climax with several fun callbacks  to the original classic and compared to  the ending that appears on the page in  the leaked script the one we saw gives  us a lot more payoff leaving Michael  Myers is fade a lot more open-ended  because as we learn in movies like Jaws  and in carpenter's classic it's always  scarier to keep the monster out of frame  keep us guessing but my question for you  is which ending do you prefer the final  cut ending that we saw in the movie or  the original ending that we now read in  the script comment down below with your  thoughts and follow me on twitter and  instagram at a basa and subscribe to me  rock stars for deep dives of everything  that you love horror movies and Marvel  and Star Wars Game of Thrones and to  thank you for sticking around to the end  of this video here is a bonus sneak peek  at this video's original alternate  ending thanks for watching everyone and  uh here's my audition for The Voice  watches over me  what no we're not gonna reshoot this mmm  yeah yeah you were right to take that  out  [Music]

